stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  breast  right   the tumor cells stain for estrogen recpetor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  10 aug 98 at 13 42 gross description  received fresh in the frozen section lab   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name and unit number  and  left axillary sentinel node  is a removed_date x removed_date x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue which is inked and bisected to reveal a brown focally yellow cut surface  one fourth is frozen as fx 1  which is resubmitted in cassette a  the remainder of the tissue is submitted in cassettes b   c  received fresh   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name and unit number  and  left simple mastectomy  is a removed_date x removed_date x 3 0cm left mastectomy specimen partially covered by a removed_date x 4 0cm grossly unremarkable ellipse of skin centered by a grossly unremarkable 1 0cm nipple  